---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Background information about Nathan Nguyen's computer science interests, goals, and hobbies."
  stylesheets={["/styles/about.css"]}
  scripts={["/js/pokemon-fact.js"]}
>
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <picture>
    <source srcset="/assets/images/grad.jpg" type="image/jpeg">
    <img src="/assets/images/placeholder.svg" alt="Portrait photo of Nathan Nguyen at graduation standing next to his girlfriend.">
  </picture>

  <section id="background">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      I am a recent UC San Diego computer science graduate with an interest
      in building software that is practical, maintainable, and clearly
      documented. Through coursework and project-based development, I have
      worked on problems that require careful planning, debugging, and
      communication of technical decisions.
    </p>
    <p>
      My academic background has helped me develop a strong foundation in
      programming fundamentals, data organization, web technologies, and
      software design. I value readable code, reliable systems, and the
      ability to explain technical work in a way that supports collaboration
      and long-term maintenance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="education">
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <article>
      <h3>University of California San Diego</h3>
      <p><strong>Bachelor of Science in Computer Science</strong></p>
      <p>
        Completed upper-division computer science coursework with a focus on
        machine learning/AI, computer security, web development, and data organization.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Diablo Valley College</h3>
      <p><strong>Associate of Science in Computer Science</strong></p>
      <p>
        Completed transfer coursework before UC San Diego, building a
        foundation in programming, mathematics, and core computer science
        concepts.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="relevant-courses">
    <h2>Relevant Courses</h2>
    <article>
      <h3>CSE 134 - Web Client Languages</h3>
      <p>
        This class focused on building web pages with clear structure,
        accessible markup, and browser based technologies.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>CSE 135 - Online Database Analytics Applications</h3>
      <p>
        This class covered the fundamentals of backend development.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>More Classes</h3>
      <p>
        I'll add the descriptions later.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="technical-interests">
    <h2>Technical Interests</h2>
    <p>
      I am interested in building useful programs that solve practical
      problems and make information easier to work with. That interest
      naturally extends into <em>web development</em> and <i>plugins</i>, where I enjoy creating
      applications that are clear, reliable, and easy to maintain.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am also developing a deeper focus on <em>machine learning</em>, homelabs,
      server networking, and <em>cybersecurity</em>. Machine learning lets me combine
      mathematical reasoning, data analysis, and software
      implementation in systems that can identify patterns at scale. With
      homelabs and server networking, I enjoy working closer to the
      infrastructure layer by configuring machines, understanding how services
      communicate, and learning how networks stay reliable. Cybersecurity
      ties these areas together by requiring technical decisions to account
      for trust, risk, and the protection of users from the beginning.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="location-context">
    <h2>Location Context</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        I currently reside in San Diego, California.<br>
        The map below provides
        geographic context for the region where I studied at UC San Diego and
        continue to develop software projects.
      </p>
    </div>
    <iframe title="Map of the San Diego region" src="https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=-117.282%2C32.715%2C-117.115%2C32.842&amp;layer=mapnik" width="560" height="315"></iframe>
  </section>

  <section id="hobbies">
    <h2>Hobbies and Interests</h2>
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/assets/images/mooseyFront.jpg" type="image/jpeg">
      <img src="/assets/images/placeholder.svg" alt="An adorable dilute tortoiseshell cat loafing comfortably on a bed." width="800" height="450">
    </picture>
    <ul>
      <li>Airsoft</li>
      <li>Cats</li>
      <li>Comics</li>
      <li>Cooking</li>
      <li>DC</li>
      <li>Hiking</li>
      <li>Marvel</li>
      <li>PC building</li>
      <li>Pokemon</li>
      <li>Star Wars</li>
      <li>Video games</li>
    </ul>
    <pokemon-fact-card heading="Pokemon Fact">
      <p>
        Pokemon facts need JavaScript and network access. When unavailable,
        this area remains a simple hobbies section.
      </p>
    </pokemon-fact-card>
    <template id="pokemon-fact-template">
      <article>
        <h3 data-role="heading">Pokemon Fact</h3>
        <dl data-role="record">
          <dt>Fact</dt>
          <dd data-role="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">
            Press the button to load a random Pokemon fact.
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <button type="button" data-role="load-button">Get Pokemon Fact</button>
      </article>
    </template>
  </section>

  <noscript>
    <p>
      JavaScript is disabled. The portfolio content and navigation remain
      available, but the theme picker cannot override your system color
      scheme without JavaScript.
    </p>
  </noscript>
</BaseLayout>
